      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the execution role and it definitely has that policy attached. i also looked at the s3 bucket policy and it doesn't have any explicit denies, but i'm still getting the error. could it be that i'm missing a permission for the bucket itself and not just the objects? like do i need to include the bucket arn without the /* at the end too? i'm a bit confused about how the resource part works for different actions.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you are hitting on a very common pitfall, which is how AWS handles resource ARNs for different actions. If you are getting access denied even with `PutObject` on the objects (`/*`), you might need to grant permissions directly on the bucket resource itself. It's a good practice to include both the object ARN and the bucket ARN in your resource list, like adding `\"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket\"` alongside `\"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"`. This covers both listing/bucket-level operations and object-level operations.",
      "source": "target",
